KNOWNBUG
contract.sol
--contract H --bound --no-standard-checks --unwind 4 --no-unwinding-assertions
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
# T1.1 Stage S3: clone walker now copies dyn-array length+elements per
# instance — sister test esol_clone_dynamic_array_isolation_pass
# CORE-passes — but this test pushes 2 elements then asserts both
# round-trip through clone.  The XOR-based hash-fold
# _ESBMC_dynarr_idx is not collision-resistant against adversarial
# nondet addresses: the SMT solver picks clone.addr such that the
# fold of clone.addr with index 1 collides with another slot, forging
# a CEX where clone.get with index 1 returns an adversarial value.
# Robust fix: switch the SMT-array shape from 1D fold-keyed to 2D
# addr-then-index — tracked as a T1.1 follow-up.
# Property holds at low --unwind 1-2 where fewer instances exist and
# the solver has less freedom to find collisions.
